#-index-name: Korean, contracted, 2020
#-display-name: Korean contracted braille (2020 standard)
#
#+language: ko
#+type: literary
#+contraction: full
#+grade: 2
#+version: 2020
# Back-translation is not implemented yet; only forward translation is
# validated.
#+direction: forward
#
# Implements the Korean Braille Standard (한국 점자 규정)
# as specified in 문화체육관광부 고시 제2020-38호 (effective 2020).
# Reference: https://www.law.go.kr/행정규칙/한국점자규정
#
# Validated against the NIKL Korean-Braille Parallel Corpus
# (국립국어원 한국어-점자 병렬 말뭉치, https://corpus.korean.go.kr/),
# which is transcribed according to the 2020 standard: forward
# translation reproduces the corpus transcription for more than 99.99%
# of the unique Hangul words and for 91% of the full sentences
# (287,916 sentences, including Roman letters, numbers and
# punctuation).
#
# Implemented rules (article numbers follow the 2020 standard):
#   제1-8항         letters (자모): onsets, codas, vowels, ㅇ omission,
#                   된소리표
#   제9항           standalone letters (단독 자모, 온표 ⠿)
#   제10-11항       vowel separators (붙임표) in vowel sequences
#   제12-16항       letter contractions (약자), including 것/껏 and
#                   된소리 combinations
#   제17항          context-dependent contraction suppression
#   제18항          word abbreviations (약어, 7 conjunctions)
#   제19·21·25항    archaic letters (옛 글자)
#   제29항          Roman letters (as in UEB) and capital letter
#                   indicators
#   제30항, 제32-35항  Roman letter passage indicators (로마자표/
#                   종료표) and when they are omitted
#   제37항          numbers
#   제6장           punctuation, including quotation marks
#                   (제52-53항)
#
# Table structure: the rules are split over several included files so
# that the hand-written rules stay reviewable next to the two large
# machine-generated blocks.
#
#   ko-2020-base.cti          hand-written: numbers, punctuation,
#                             capital-letter and Roman-letter passage
#                             machinery
#   ko-2020-jamo.cti          hand-written: standalone jamo (온표) and
#                             archaic letters (옛 글자)
#   ko-2020-ueb-contractions.cti  UEB grade-2 contractions for Roman
#                             letter sequences, derived from
#                             en-ueb-g2.ctb (see the header of that
#                             file)
#   ko-2020-context.cti       machine-generated: context rules for
#                             contraction suppression and vowel
#                             separators (제17항, 제10-11항)
#   ko-2020-syllables.cti     machine-generated: mappings for all
#                             11,172 Hangul syllables
#   ko-2020-word-abbr.cti     hand-written: word abbreviations (제18항)
#
# The machine-generated files are derived from the hand-written clause
# rules; please do not edit them by hand.

include ko-2020-base.cti
include ko-2020-jamo.cti
# 제29항: Roman letters are written as in UEB — grade-2 contractions
# included (confirmed against the NIKL corpus)
include ko-2020-ueb-contractions.cti
include ko-2020-context.cti
include ko-2020-syllables.cti
include ko-2020-word-abbr.cti
